  "body": "**domenic**\r\n\r\n_Sorry, we disagree, for the reasons explained in the HTML Standard. We have no plans to change this, so I'll close this issue._\r\n\r\nWhere in the standard does it give reasons for not referring to ECMAScript as JavaScript?\r\n\r\n\r\n_(for what it's worth, I do agree that using two names for the same product is confusing. I just disagree that the way to address this is to switch to the less-common name.)_\r\n\r\nThere is no other way so it's either fix it, or keep calling an apple an orange. It's as simple as that.",
